==Battleground==
*1 [[Manic Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Manic Eraser Cat]] spawns.
*1 [[Manic Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Manic Eraser Cat]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*4 [[Midnite D.|Midnite Ds]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Using [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]], you're able to cheese this stage just like the original [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 32|Floor 32]], although the additions of Sir Rel and Midnite D. makes this strategy more difficult. [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] works well as a meatshield here, since the main pushers are all its target traits. [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]] can deal good damage to the Midnite D./Sir Rels when stacked. Try to get Cat God to brute force Midnite D's Shield; once broken, an [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] hit should be enough to send him back. [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]] (True Form recommended, but all forms work) can also be extremely valuable here as he has a one slot Knockback [[Cat Combo]] as well as a guaranteed knockback against every enemy (with Slow included in True Form).
A good set of meatshields to spam for this include [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]], [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], as it activates the [[Rich and Poor (Combo)|Rich and Poor]], and if you use [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]] you can also activate the
[[Mo' Hawks (Combo)|Mo' Hawks]], giving an extra boost to your knockback abilities and giving a bit more cash to start with.

